{
  "_schema": "item_id -> { name, use: eat|drink|tool|build, hunger/thirst: restore amounts, side_effect, melee_damage/melee_reach/swing_sec for weapons, and for worn gear: worn + the field naming its effect (pack_slots | light | cold_relief). The 'effect' string names the code that implements it — worn gear with no implementation is a lie. PlayerState.use_hotbar implements hunger/thirst/comfort/side_effect; scripts/components/item_effects.gd implements FOUR more on the same consume path: heal (adds to the 0..1 life bar), cures ('sickness'), warmth, returns (item id handed back when the consumable is spent — how a drunk bottle leaves you the bottle), plus an optional 'line' overriding the toast. NOTE: only an eat/drink item is ever SPENT by use_hotbar, so a consumable that is not food carries use:drink with thirst 0. Water vessels add vessel:true + vessel_kind (bottle|flask) + fills_to + fill_hours, read by scripts/components/rain_catcher.gd.",
